  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MARINE TURTLES MONITORING AND PROTECTION IN THE REPUBLIC OF CONGO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO PROTECT SEA TURTLE NESTING POPULATIONS ON 50 KM OF NESTING BEACHES WITHIN CONKOUATI- DOUALI NATIONAL PARK, AND 47 KM OF NESTING BEACH OUTSIDE THE PARK WHICH ARE IMPORTANT NESTING BEACHES FOR THE WEST AFRICA LEATHERBACK NESTING POPULATION AND ATLANTIC NESTING POPULATION OF OLIVE RIDLEYS. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) DAILY SURVEYS BY COMMUNITY MEMBERS FROM LOCAL VILLAGES ON 86 KM OF NESTING BEACH TO COUNT NESTS AND DETER POACHING (2) WORK COLLABORATIVELY WITH FISHERS TO SAFELY RELEASE SEA TURTLES ACCIDENTLY CAPTURED IN GILL NETS ON IMPORTANT FORAGING GROUNDS THAT RESULTS IN THE RELEASE OF OVER 1,500 TURTLES ANNUALLY (3) OUTREACH AND EDUCATION WITH LOCAL COMMUNITIES INCLUDING SCHOOL PROGRAMS, TV AND RADIO SHOWS AND ENVIRONMENTAL FESTIVALS.</narrative>
  </description>
